        {
          "_key": "obbxn1es",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Verdict: Midjourney wins on image quality. Lovart wins on everything that happens after the image is generated. For standalone AI artists, Midjourney. For creators who make things with AI images, Lovart."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "ef5vqh4u",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "2k1ixuqm",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Can I use Lovart with other AI models?"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "3nwv8380",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "bfz6uhs0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Yes — Lovart Imagine routes prompts to multiple underlying models depending on the task. For specific model preferences, Lovart Pro allows model selection in advanced mode. You're not locked into a single AI engine."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "2h3abc6a",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "l8v3boxn",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For creators who want both Lovart's workflow and Midjourney's image quality: generate in Midjourney → import to Lovart for design, templating, and export. Multi-platform workflows are standard practice."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "49x8tfg2",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "wtb8xwkv",
          "_type": "span",
